      "slip_behavior": null,
      "phase_evolution": "α → α + FCC Cu-rich phase → α-Mn + β-Mn + BCC phase → β-Mn + BCC phase + FCC Cu-rich phase",
      "interface_notes": "For the 19Al alloy aged at ≥600 °C the α matrix is almost completely transformed into β-Mn after just 1 h of aging and numerous fine precipitates are distributed within the β-Mn; the volume fraction of these FCC Cu-rich + BCC precipitates between the β-Mn interfaces increases with Al content, which lowers the absolute volume fraction of β-Mn and the overall hardness. The FCC Cu-rich phase is the more ductile constituent (the BCC phase is harder), so the decrease of the ductile FCC Cu-rich phase between β-Mn interfaces with increasing Al content lowers the fracture toughness."
    }
